  "final": {
    "agentMessage": "My intention: Find out how to renew at a DMV office instead of online, and how to save time on the office visit.\n\nOn the mockup page \"Driver's License Online Renewal & Appointments\":\n\n**Renew in Person at an Office - Short answer:**\n> You can renew at a local office instead of online. To save time on your office visit, bring your notice and documents and complete any available pre-application worksheet in advance.\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Choose an office location and time that works for you.\n2. Bring your renewal notice, current license, and any documents listed for your renewal type.\n3. Check in on arrival and follow staff directions for photo and review.\n\n**Tip for a shorter office visit:**\ndouble-check your papers the night before and arrive a little early for your time slot.\n\n**Appointments - How to schedule (to save time):**\nShort answer: Appointments are scheduled through the official appointment system. Choose service type, location, and time, then save your confirmation.\n\n1. Select \"driver's license renewal\" as the service reason.\n2. Enter your ZIP or county to see nearby offices.\n3. Pick a date and time and save the confirmation details.\n\nIf no times are available, try another nearby office or check back later. You can reschedule or cancel with your confirmation information.\n\nThis answers renewing in-person instead of online and saving time: book ahead, bring notice + documents, do pre-application, arrive early."
